{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ImplicitDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Row","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Row","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Sequence","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:ST"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Row","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:ST7ElementQa"},{"text":" == ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It is a lawful ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"text":", so every generic algorithm runs on it, including those that need","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the whole vertex set (components, centrality), with no edge storage.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For a state space with no vertex collection (an unbounded grid, a puzzle), use the closure"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"searches instead: Traversal’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"breadthFirstSearch(from:successors:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and ShortestPaths’"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dijkstraShortestPath(from:cutoff:successors:success:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"aStarShortestPath(from:cutoff: successors:heuristic:success:)"},{"type":"text","text":". For "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":" states over a finite set, number them and use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LabeledGraph<State, ImplicitDirectedGraph<Row>>"},{"type":"text","text":". A grid is numbered row-major."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"The-closure","text":"The closure"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"successors(v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" lists the targets of the edges leaving "},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", once per edge, as any"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"Sequence<Int>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", such as an array or a lazy filter over a fixed neighbor list. A specialized"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"build inlines it with no type erasure. Each read of a row calls it once. "},{"code":"successors(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"outEdges(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"outDegree(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"contains(edge:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" call it once each, and "},{"code":"edges","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"edgeCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" once per vertex."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The closure must return the same sequence each time it is asked about the same vertex. This is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not checked, and a closure that breaks it breaks every algorithm. Each target is checked to be a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex when it is read, not when the row is formed.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"On a hot path, return a small struct that computes the row up front into fixed slots and yields"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them by count. A "},{"code":"lazy.filter","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" calls its predicate per element and carries the unfiltered"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"iterator’s state, which costs more per edge."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Positions","text":"Positions"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An edge’s position is "},{"code":"Edges.Index","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which holds its source, its rank in the source’s row, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its target. Equality, order and hashing use "},{"code":"(source, rank)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which is unique even among"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"parallel edges and self-loops. Because the position carries the target, "},{"code":"source(ofEdgeAt:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"target(ofEdgeAt:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and a weight closure reading "},{"code":"$0.target","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" call nothing. There are no dense"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edge indices."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Attached-values","text":"Attached values"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The graph is not a ","type":"text"},{"code":"PropertyGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", because ","type":"text"},{"code":"(source, rank)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" has a dense offset only after every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"earlier row is counted. Keep vertex values in an array of ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertexCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" indexed by vertex, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"compute edge values from the position (","type":"text"},{"code":"$0.source","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"$0.target","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The graph is not ","type":"text"},{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", because a closure has no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"identity and is not ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph"},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/OutEdges","doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/Successors"],"generated":true,"title":"Structures","anchor":"Structures"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/init(vertexCount:successors:)"],"generated":true,"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/generation"],"generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties","anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/outDegree(checked:)","doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/outEdges(checked:)","doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/successors(checked:)","doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/vertexIndex(checked:)"],"generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods","anchor":"Instance-Methods"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/DirectedGraph-Implementations"],"generated":true,"title":"Default Implementations","anchor":"Default-Implementations"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/docum